## The one finding to fix

Ship Gate row 5 requires `go test ./internal/importer/... ./internal/utils/... ./cmd/bd/...` to exit 0. It exits 1 because `TestDaemonAutoStart/shouldAutoStartDaemon_defaults_to_true` in `cmd/bd/autostart_test.go` fails. The item cannot ship with a red suite, so the test gets fixed here even though the failure predates this item.

Root cause: the test calls `config.Initialize()` from the package directory, and config discovery walks up to this repo's own committed `.beads/config.yaml`, which sets `auto-start-daemon: false` (w28, commit a5ce30c1b, a deliberate fleet-wide decision that stays). The test asserts a built-in default while reading a real config file, so it is not isolated from its host repo. The sibling test `TestShouldAutoStartDaemonWorktreeIntegration` in `cmd/bd/worktree_daemon_test.go:166` shows the isolation pattern already used in this package: change into a directory with no `.beads/config.yaml` on any ancestor path, re-run `config.Initialize()`, and restore cwd plus config on exit.

Fix the test's isolation, not the assertion and not the repo config: run `TestDaemonAutoStart` from a fresh `t.TempDir()` (chdir in, `config.Initialize()`, defer chdir back plus `config.Initialize()`). Check whether other tests in `cmd/bd` that read the built-in default suffer the same dependency on the host repo's config and would fail the same way; if a helper already exists for this, use it rather than duplicating. Keep the change minimal and in test files only.

## Acceptance
1. `cd cmd/bd && go test -run 'TestDaemonAutoStart' ./` passes. Log to `/home/ben/worktrees/beads/w4_id-ownership/work/w4_id-ownership/builds/r2-step1.log`.
2. `go test ./internal/importer/... ./internal/utils/... ./cmd/bd/...` from the worktree root exits 0 with every package `ok`. Log to `/home/ben/worktrees/beads/w4_id-ownership/work/w4_id-ownership/builds/r2-step2.log`. Set `BEADS_NO_DAEMON=1 BD_NO_DAEMON=true` in the shell as before.

